Changes in version 1.25.1 (2026-04-16)
- Use `BiocParallel` instead of `doParallel` / `foreach`
- Internal: decouple I/O from FIR integration; `integrateFIR()` now accepts pre-extracted signal (`FIR_data`) instead of a raw `OnDiskMSnExp` handle
- Internal: reuse already-extracted ROI signal when FIR windows are contained within ROI bounds, avoiding a redundant raw-data read
- `peakPantheR_parallelAnnotation()` reuses cached `@dataPoints`/`@TIC`/`@acquisitionTime` when re-annotating an already-annotated object, skipping per-file disk reads for re-fit workflows. Per-file fallback to disk when the cache is missing or malformed
- New `peakPantheR_updateAnnotationParamsCSV()`: overlay ROI (and optionally uROI / FIR) from a CSV onto an existing `peakPantheRAnnotation`, preserving cached `@dataPoints` / `@TIC` / `@acquisitionTime` so the next `peakPantheR_parallelAnnotation()` refits without re-reading raw spectra
- Documentation: `@ROI`, `@uROI` and `@FIR` are now explicitly framed as *extraction envelope* (cache key, read from disk), *integration window* (searched by `findTargetFeatures`, user-mutable on refit) and *fallback integration region* (used when `useFIR = TRUE` and a fit fails), respectively. Invariant: `uROI ⊆ ROI` and `FIR ⊆ ROI`. `useFIR` is a NA-vs-fill toggle; `useUROI` is phased for deprecation
- Construction: `@uROI` and `@FIR` are seeded from `@ROI` when not supplied, and `@uROIExist` / `@useUROI` default to `TRUE` (behaviourally identical to the prior defaults, since an unset `@uROI` now mirrors `@ROI`)
- Cache: `peakPantheR_parallelAnnotation()` now geometrically checks that each cached EIC spans the current target bounds (`target ⊆ @ROI`); mismatches fall back to a fresh disk read instead of silently truncating
- `peakPantheR_updateAnnotationParamsCSV()`: basic-layout CSVs now update `@uROI` and `@FIR` (leaving `@ROI` as the stable cache key) by default. Pass `target = "ROI"` for the legacy behaviour; a deprecation message is emitted
- `annotationDiagnosticPlots()`: new `plotWindow` argument (`"uROI"` default, `"ROI"` for the full extraction envelope) controls the EIC x-axis range in the diagnostic plots
- `peakPantheRAnnotation()`: passing `useUROI` now emits a soft deprecation message. `@uROI` is always the integration target once seeded; the flag will be removed in a future release. `useFIR` is unchanged
- GUI: "Refit this compound" now reliably picks up drag-edited `@uROI` / `@FIR` bounds. `apply_rt_window_to_annotation()` flips `@useUROI` / `@uROIExist` when `"uROI"` is edited and `@useFIR` when `"FIR"` is edited, so the refit path no longer falls back to the original `@ROI`
- GUI: the interactive diagnostic EIC plot now renders the full `@ROI` extraction envelope (was previously restricted to `@uROI`), with `@uROI` / `@FIR` overlaid as shaded bands
- GUI: new *X-axis range* toggle on the diagnostic plot control strip switches between the full `@ROI` envelope and the `@uROI`/`@FIR` union; the y-axis rescales to the EIC intensity observed inside the zoomed window so tall peaks outside do not flatten the signal of interest. Purely a view-range change, the EIC data remains extracted over `@ROI`
- GUI: RT correction — selecting the `constant` method now exposes a reference-compound picker and refuses to run without exactly one reference selected. Previously the constant-shift branch silently fell through with all compounds as "references" and mis-sized `correctedRt` / `predictedRtDrift` vectors
- GUI: diagnostic plot control strip no longer resets the *Number of Samples to show*, *Colour by Sample Metadata*, or *Sample mode* when the annotation mutates (refit, drag-select, Suggest uROI/FIR, FIR = uROI). The sample count now defaults to `min(50, nbSamples)` on first render to avoid flooding the plot with hundreds of EICs
- `peakPantheR_applyRTCorrection()` / `retentionTimeCorrection()`: fix sign bug in the corrected rt. `rt_dev_sec = measured - expected`, so the corrected expected rt is now `rt + predictedDrift` (previously `rt - predictedDrift`), which moves the GUI's red target line onto the observed peak instead of away from it. Downstream `@uROI` / `@FIR` rt windows shift accordingly
- `peakPantheR_singleFileSearch()` gains a `cacheROI` argument that decouples the disk-extraction / cache envelope from the curve-fit window. `peakPantheR_parallelAnnotation()` now always passes `@ROI` as the cache envelope, so `@dataPoints` is preserved at the full `@ROI` across refits. Diagnostic plots keep their surrounding EIC context and cached refits no longer degrade when `@uROI` is narrowed. FIR windows contained in `@ROI` are now served from the widened cached data without a separate disk read. The single `cacheROI` parameter replaces the earlier split (`extractionROI` + `cachedROI`); the unused `cachedTIC` / `cachedAcquTime` kwargs are removed (the parallel pipeline preserves TIC / acquisitionTime for cache hits via its own mask)